// Custom event schema injects an extra reserved field
// `__drupe_sessionid` (see event.dwschema). This policy correlates on
// it: a Read is permitted only if there was formerly a Login in the SAME
// session — the past Login's `__drupe_sessionid` must equal the
// current Read's, referenced via the generic `context.<field>` path
// (`context.__drupe_sessionid` reads the request event's field of that
// name). This is an ordinary injected/declared field, not request scope,
// so it is reached by its own name (unlike `principal`).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user, __drupe_sessionid: context.__drupe_sessionid }
};
